# trivy --ignorefile — accepted by trivy for image, fs, config, and secret scans.
#
# Format:
#   - one CVE / secret ID / misconfig ID per line
#   - blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored
#   - trivy matches the ID against finding.VulnerabilityID for CVEs,
#     finding.AVDID for misconfigs, and finding.RuleID for secrets
#
# Every entry should be paired with a rationale in a comment immediately above:
#   - a JIRA / issue link, OR
#   - a one-line "why this finding is accepted" justification, AND
#   - an expiration date or "Re-check when <event>" so stale entries can be triaged
#
# Examples:
#
#   # https://example.atlassian.net/browse/SEC-1234
#   # Accepted: not exploitable in our network topology. Re-check: 2026-12-31.
#   CVE-2024-12345
#
#   # Re-check when we move off the old Spring Boot 3.1 BOM.
#   CVE-2024-67890
#
# Honored by:  trivy (image / fs / config / secret) via `--ignorefile <path>`
# Generated by: scanImages / scanSource / scanConfig / scanSecrets / scanReferencedImages
